.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-ports-checkout
command checks out or clones a ports tree matching the current
package branch, i.e. a quarterly snapshot or latest (HEAD).
Shallow clones are used where available to save time and disk space.
For a full clone, follow the instructions provided by your operating
system.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

